{
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "$id": "https://apk.audio/schemas/analyzer-peak/1.1.0",
  "title": "analyzer-peak — the Scanalyzer analyzer's .PEAK, in both of its shapes",
  "description": "The record oa_sample_analyzer writes: one per audio file by `Encoders/sidecar.rs::write_sidecar` (an OBJECT, `<sample>.PEAK`) and all of them together by `Pipeline/run.rs` (an ARRAY, `sample_cloud_data.PEAK`), and the `result` of a Worker-SAMPLE_ANALYZER job (sample_analyzer/incoming/result, the OBJECT). OWNED HERE, by PROCESSOR.SampleAnalyzer (`schema/peak.schema.json`, compiled in as `oa_sample_analyzer::schema::PEAK_SCHEMA`); it lived in SCANALYZER.Like.audio as `Web_Front/src/analyzerPeakSchema.json` until the 2026-10-30 audit moved it to the format's owner, and readers there now take it through the crate. `metadata.format` = `schema::PEAK_FORMAT`, `metadata.schema_version` = `schema::PEAK_SCHEMA_VERSION` (the semver in the $id). Tests: an analysed record and the worker's result validate (`src/Core/schema.rs`, `SRC/src/lib.rs`); Scanalyzer's `wasm_analyzer` validates every tracked `.PEAK` it reads. Originally written off the 147 tracked `.PEAK` (346 records) of 2026-09-09 — PLAN-907.01. The extension `.PEAK` names four documents and this schema types two of them; the discriminator table is in `$comment`.",
  "$comment": "WHAT `.PEAK` MEANS, PER WRITER. The extension is borrowed: it began life as a Pro Tools WAVEFORM PEAK CACHE, and 856 of those were untracked from this repository in August 2026. Nothing here is a waveform cache, and only ONE of the four carries waveform peaks at all — this one, base64 in `preview.peak_data_base64`.\n\n  1. analyzer per-file sidecar   OBJECT, this schema. Discriminator: `metadata.analyzer_version`. 144 tracked.\n  2. analyzer aggregate / cloud  ARRAY of (1), this schema. Discriminator: a JSON array whose first element is (1). 3 tracked: two `sample_cloud_data.PEAK` and one `samples.PEAK`, 202 records between them. This is the corpus `peakSchema.ts` exists to read; it is not a fossil.\n  3. peak-lens-sidecar          OBJECT, `lensPeakSidecarSchema.json` in SCANALYZER.Like.audio `Web_Front/src/`. Discriminator: `format: \"peak-lens-sidecar\"`. Downloaded by a visitor; never tracked.\n  4. extract_note_root_beat_map.py's write   OBJECT. NOT A FOURTH FORMAT — it is (1) with 2 of its 10 groups, written to (1)'s own path, and the one thing it adds (`musicality.note_root_key_beat_marker_map`) is a field (1) already carries in 164 of 346 records because `Scananalyzers/Musical/note_map.rs` is a port of that same CLI. Never tracked.\n\nTWO GROUP NAMES COLLIDE ACROSS (1) AND (3) WITH ZERO FIELDS IN COMMON. `musicality` here is {pitch_hz, root_note_name, root_frequency_hz, root_cents_offset, beats_per_minute, root_midi_note, chromagram, ...}; in the lens sidecar it is {key, keyConfidence, pitchHz, centsOffset, bpm}. `ucs` here is {category, subcategory, id, confidence, alternatives, synonyms, reason}; there it is {cat_key, creator_id, source_id}. A reader that branches on a group NAME gets the wrong document with no error. That is why the discriminator is `metadata.analyzer_version` and not a group.\n\nTHERE IS NOW A `format` FIELD, AND THE TRACKED CORPUS DOES NOT CARRY IT YET. `peak::Metadata` gained `format` and `schema_version` on 2026-09-10 (PLAN-1070.01), so everything the analyzer writes from now on declares itself: `analyzer-peak`, and the semver in the $id above. The 147 tracked `.PEAK` predate that and read back with both fields EMPTY, deliberately — `#[serde(default)]` hands them the empty string rather than the constant, because a record must not come back claiming a declaration it never made. That is why both keys are OPTIONAL here and their `enum` admits the empty string: the migration is a re-scan of `SAMPLE and PLAY/SampleLibrary/` with the release binary and one commit of 147 regenerated files, and when that lands the empty string comes out of both enums and both keys join `required`. Until then a reader that finds neither key falls back to the discriminator it always had — the `metadata` group's PRESENCE — which is what the two readers still branch on.\n\nSTRICTNESS IS THE POINT. `additionalProperties: false` with a complete `required` at every level is what turns a field added, renamed or dropped in `Core/peak.rs` into a red lane instead of a silent shape change — the same instrument `perfSchema.json` uses, and the omission `peakSchema.ts` is 115 lines of aftermath from. `required` here means PRESENT IN ALL 346 RECORDS; a key absent from some is optional because older records predate it (`analysis_depth`, `preview`, `envelope.slices`: 226; `true_peak_dbtp`, `loudness_range_lu`, `note_root_key_beat_marker_map`: 164; `bioacoustic_syntax`: 18).",
  "oneOf": [
